  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Finland&#xB4;s Pre-Departure Orientation Programme 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this project is to contribute to the early integration of approximately 600 beneficiaries selected for resettlement to Finland from Iran (the Islamic Republic of), Peru, Rwanda, T&#xFC;rkiye and Zambia by providing a comprehensive Pre-Departure Orientation (PDO) training to refugees before their departure. 
 
IOM aims to achieve the project&#x2019;s objective by working towards enabling beneficiaries to develop practical skills and attitudes that contribute to their early integration in their receiving communities in Finland. More specifically, the project will provide PDO trainings that empower quota refugees through developing their knowledge of Finnish society and providing them with accurate information and support in an age-, gender- and context-specific manner. In addition to the provision of PDO trainings, IOM will also update essential learning and self-study materials such as the &#x201C;Moving to Finland&#x201D; website and &#x201C;Moving to Finland&#x201D; -workbook to enable beneficiaries to continue their learning process after the PDO sessions have been held.</narrative>
  </description>
